[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3178054322","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109514#issuecomment-3178054322","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109514","id":3178054322,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc69bUKy","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-12T07:27:40Z","updated_at":"2025-08-12T07:27:40Z","body":"Just for a historical note, the adding everything to the origin in the BVH, then moving paradigm is something we noticed as problematic a while ago (circa 2020?) around when I was writing the BVH used for physics and rendering in 3.x (this was since replaced for rendering in 4.x by Juan's \"dynamic BVH\"). PouleyKetchoup did a fair bit of research into this if I remember right when he was maintaining physics but some of these issues / PRs may have been deleted (can't find them now by searching, but will post if I can find).\r\n\r\nThe issue was not just adding to the BVH itself, it was that you would get pairings of every combination at the origin (which scales with `O(N squared)` or something like that). Pairings would occur and affect lighting, shadows, collision detection, etc etc.\r\n\r\nAs far as processing the better solution would be add the object, move to initial location, _then_ activate in the BVH. But this had compat breaking implications. Pouley left the project before we fixed up any of this.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3178054322/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":4},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3180379425","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109514#issuecomment-3180379425","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109514","id":3180379425,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc69kL0h","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-12T17:46:06Z","updated_at":"2025-08-12T17:46:06Z","body":"> I also wrote up some code to just run the BVH outside of a project, and tested that by itself. The benchmark inserts 25,000 nodes into a BVH in a variety of patterns.\r\n\r\nIs this code available somewhere so I can run it locally? (You could upload it to a separate branch, for instance.)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3180379425/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3187083767","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109514#issuecomment-3187083767","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109514","id":3187083767,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc699wn3","user":{"login":"precup","id":709680,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwOTY4MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/709680?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup","html_url":"https://github.com/precup","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-14T06:08:15Z","updated_at":"2025-08-14T06:08:15Z","body":"> Is this code available somewhere so I can run it locally? (You could upload it to a separate branch, for instance.)\r\n\r\nI pushed it to [precup:bvh-benchmark](https://github.com/precup/godot/tree/bvh-benchmark). It's ugly, sorry. It's also set up a bit differently than the one I originally used because I had been using it to test other options, but the core benchmark is the same. It's currently set up to get numbers on `insert` time changes. If you want to see evidence of the bad case, uncomment the other benchmark calls and drop the trials to like 10.\r\n\r\nI'll note for posterity in case anyone's curious: I had more recently tried two other solutions to get the cost lower, and neither worked. One was adding `unlikely` to the condition, which slowed inserts down by an additional 1%, and the other was using `fpclassify` to try to cheapen both comparisons, which added an additional 2%.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3187083767/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3511079303","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109514#issuecomment-3511079303","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109514","id":3511079303,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7RRtGH","user":{"login":"Saul2022","id":97898580,"node_id":"U_kgDOBdXQVA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97898580?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022","html_url":"https://github.com/Saul2022","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/repos","events_ur